&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#160; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 13.3333px;"&gt;The change in the Transmission Plant is due to regular CWIP closures to Utility Plant as well as additions for the increased ARO Revision as as noted in Note 7. It should be noted that the ARO Revision is considered Non-cash activity. In the 2025, construction in progress value, $495,210 are non-cash investing activities related to capital accruals.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '4'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.66pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;4.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.66pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Regulatory assets and regulatory liabilities&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Regulatory Assets and Regulatory Liabilities include shipper/Operational Balancing Agreements imbalances, lost and unaccounted for gas ("LAUF") and excess deferred tax adjustments related to the new law under H.R. 1 which changed the tax rates going forward.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On December 31, 2025 and 2024, Regulatory Assets totaled $3,351,874 and $4,354,596, respectively. On December 31, 2025 and 2024, Regulatory Liabilities totaled $1,148,990 and $1,339,713, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On December 31, 2017, the change in income tax rate resulted in a reduction in net Deferred Income Tax Liability, the recognition of a new Regulatory Liability of $1,040,245 and a new Regulatory Asset of $521,633 which is shown as part of the total balances in above paragraph.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;These balances related to excess deferred tax began to be amortized down to deferred tax expenses during the year 2019 for a net of $6,286.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The 2025 amortization was for a net of $6,286 which left remaining balances in the Regulatory Liability account of $978,351 and the Regulatory Asset of $503,741.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: '%0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '5'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 9.66pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;5.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 9.66pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Provision for Income Taxes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;A reconciliation of the Company's provision for income taxes calculated at the federal statutory rate to the actual income tax provision recorded for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 is as follows:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
